[line]

[size=4][b][color=#1084D0]Why this one[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]One DLL, nothing else.[/b] No UE4SS, no Cheat Engine, no launcher, no Visual C++ redistributable. No game file is modified: uninstalling is deleting the file.
[*][b]Five mods, one file, no stutter.[/b] The UE4SS versions scanned every object in the game dozens of times a second; the native ports look things up once and cache them. The minimap moves by render translation instead of re-laying out a 4K widget every frame.
[*][b]Safer than the originals.[/b] The keypad fix that crashed the game, the flashlight fix that froze it: both rewritten and audited (see KETAMINE++.md in the download).
[*][b]Update-proof by design.[/b] Everything is found by name at runtime. If an update removes something, that option greys out with the reason instead of crashing.
[*][b]Open source (MIT).[/b] Full source on GitHub, build it yourself if you like.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#1084D0]Full feature list[/color][/b][/size]
[spoiler]
[b]Player[/b]
[list]
[*]God mode, infinite health, set your health to any value
[*]No sprint cooldown, invisible to enemies
[*]One-hit kill, damage multiplier
[/list]
[b]Combat[/b]
[list]
[*]Silent aim inside an adjustable circle (the circle is hidden by default)
[*]Infinite ammo, unbreakable melee weapons
[*]Genesis Configuration: shows what your save has; powers with no Suffering cost and no cooldown (off at every load, turn them on when you want), refill Suffering, unlock Telekinesis, Pyrokinesis and Hellchains early
[/list]
[b]Movement[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Jump[/b] on a key of your choice (the game has none), height x1.2 by default
[*][b]Bunny hop[/b]: manual timing (press jump as you land: +10%, perfect within 30 ms: +20%) or auto hop, momentum carried in every direction, air strafing, no speed cap
[*][b]Speedometer[/b] and hop readout in km/h, mph, hammer units or Unreal units
[*]Look straight up and down (the game stops at 60° / 70°)
[*]Fly, noclip, free camera (with pause time), speed multiplier, saved positions, teleport to checkpoints
[/list]
[b]FOV editor[/b] (TrueFOV)
[list]
[*]World FOV, viewmodel FOV and aiming FOV, live, gameplay only (cutscenes keep theirs)
[*]Keeps the game's sprint and ladder FOV effects, scaled around yours
[*]Page Up / Page Down to step it, End to toggle
[/list]
[b]Minimap[/b] (True Minimap)
[list]
[*]Square, circle, octagon or diamond; rotates with you (forward is up) or stays north-up
[*]Size, zoom, transparency, placement, a frame in your skin's accent colour
[*]Shows where the game blocks its own map (optional), hides in the Labyrinth and behind game screens
[/list]
[b]Fixes[/b] (uwumatic101's mods, native)
[list]
[*]Keep movement after tools: WASD isn't dropped after the flashlight or a medkit
[*]Keypad input fix: no lockout after moving the cursor, number keys press the keypad buttons
[*]Speed up interactions: save point x2.5, Lament puzzle x2, reward pillars x3.5, cylinder puzzles x2, dock boat x3.5 (each has its own slider)
[*]Quick interact: shorter pickup / ladder hold, faster ladder climbing
[*]Auto-skip cutscenes (off by default; unskippable ones are left alone)
[*]Hide the "DROP [Z]" hint, the flashlight toggle and the crafting icon when the HUD goes idle
[/list]
[b]ESP[/b]
[list]
[*]Enemies: box, health bar, name, distance, skeleton, head, chams, snaplines, off-screen arrows
[*]World: items, loot containers, save points
[*]A colour for every kind of thing, independent of the skin
[/list]
[b]Inventory and progress[/b]
[list]
[*]Money, any item in any amount, weapon skins & charms
[*]Objectives: see, complete; shop level
[/list]
[b]World and UI[/b]
[list]
[*]Time scale, freeze enemies, kill enemies nearby, hide HUD
[*][b]Simple prompts[/b] (experimental): interaction prompts become plain text, [F] Barter, in your colour and size, no artwork
[*][b]KETAMINE++ in the pause menu[/b]: click it to open the menu
[/list]
[b]Settings[/b]
[list]
[*][b]18 skins + your own[/b]: Win95 (default), Black Hat, Zero Day (retro Windows, Tahoma, bevels, title bar), Phosphor, Amber CRT, Root Shell, Mainframe, Netrunner, BSOD (terminal, Consolas), KETAMINE++, KETAMINE and more (modern)
[*]A cursor drawn in the skin's style (the Windows 9x pixel arrow in retro skins)
[*]A hotkey for every switch, two menu keys (F1 and F8), 9 languages, UI scale, window opacity
[*]Skip intros, UI dump for modders, in-game credits
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#1084D0]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Vortex:[/b] click [i]Mod Manager Download[/i], enable and deploy.

[b]Manual:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]In Steam: right-click the game → [i]Manage[/i] → [i]Browse local files[/i].
[*]Open [b]Hellraiser\Binaries\Win64[/b] (next to Hellraiser-Win64-Shipping.exe).
[*]Copy [b]winmm.dll[/b] there (and [b]KetaminePlusPlus.ini[/b] if you want the default settings file; it is created anyway).
[*][b]Remove what KETAMINE++ replaces[/b]: the original Ketamine Menu or TrueFOV winmm.dll (KETAMINE++ takes its place), and the UE4SS versions of the five fixes and of True Minimap in ue4ss\Mods, so nothing runs twice. Your KetamineMenu.ini is copied over on the first start.
[*]Start the game, load a save, press [b]F1[/b] or [b]F8[/b].
[/list]

[b]Linux / Steam Deck (Proton):[/b] add this to the game's launch options so Proton loads the mod's winmm.dll:
[code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="winmm=n,b" %command%[/code]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#1084D0]First steps (tutorial)[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Open the menu[/b] with F1 or F8, the X at the top right closes it. In the pause menu, click [b]KETAMINE++[/b] under the game's own items.
[*][b]Pick a look[/b] in Settings → Skin. Win95 is the default; try Phosphor or BSOD for a terminal.
[*][b]Jump key:[/b] Space jumps, but Space is also the game's [b]Evade[/b] by default. Rebind Evade in the game's Controls, or pick another jump key in Movement → Jump key. The tab warns you if the key is taken.
[*][b]Bunny hop:[/b] manual timing by default: press jump as you land (or turn on Auto hop and hold the key); strafe and turn the mouse together in the air to build speed. Turn on the Speedometer to see it.
[*][b]FOV:[/b] the FOV tab is on by default at 120° world / 110° viewmodel / 90° aiming. Page Up / Page Down change it in game, End toggles it.
[*][b]Minimap:[/b] off by default. Turn it on in the Minimap tab; open the TAB map once in each level so it can copy it.
[*][b]Fixes:[/b] all on except cutscene skip. A future game patch may fix these itself: if one starts acting odd after an update, turn it off.
[*][b]Genesis Configuration:[/b] the Combat tab shows what your save has. "Powers cost nothing" and "No power cooldown" start off at every load; turn them on after loading.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#1084D0]Before you play[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Back up your saves: [b]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Hellraiser\Saved\SaveGames[/b]
[*]Giving key items or completing objectives can break scripted sequences: save first.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#1084D0]Compatibility[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Game 1.2.0.227791 (Steam), DirectX 12 and 11. Built to survive updates (options grey out instead of crashing).
[*]Works with ReShade (dxgi.dll) and UE4SS (dwmapi.dll). Don't run it together with the original Ketamine Menu, TrueFOV or the UE4SS versions of the bundled mods.
[*]Frame generation (DLSS-G, FSR, XeSS FG): supported; if the menu flickers, turn it off.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#1084D0]Uninstall[/color][/b][/size]
Delete winmm.dll, KetaminePlusPlus.ini and KetaminePlusPlus.log from Hellraiser\Binaries\Win64.

[size=4][b][color=#1084D0]Troubleshooting[/color][/b][/size]
[spoiler]
[b]F1 / F8 do nothing[/b]
Check that winmm.dll is in Hellraiser\Binaries\Win64. Open KetaminePlusPlus.log in the same folder: if it doesn't exist, the DLL wasn't loaded (folder or antivirus).

[b]Everything is greyed out[/b]
Load a save first. If the header says [i]Engine not hooked[/i], post in the Bugs tab with your KetaminePlusPlus.log.

[b]Something misbehaves[/b]
Turn the related option off and send KetaminePlusPlus.log (it is rewritten at every start). Settings → [i]Dump on-screen UI[/i] adds the game's widgets to the log, which helps with UI issues.

[b]My antivirus flags the DLL[/b]
Trainers hook a game's rendering and memory, which antivirus heuristics dislike. It's a false positive: the full source is on GitHub, and you can build it yourself.
[/spoiler]

